WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.610
Pedestrian deaths in Atlanta
are a public-health problem.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.533
Many of us walk between Klaus, Tech
Square, and Midtown MARTA late at night.

00:00:09.573 --> 00:00:13.654
Our friends, especially women,
already plan routes around well-lit,

00:00:13.694 --> 00:00:17.114
busier streets, and text each
other when they get home.

00:00:17.154 --> 00:00:21.653
Yet every navigation app asks
one question: what's fastest?

00:00:21.693 --> 00:00:26.030
So we built PathPro: a map of where
and when traffic risk is highest,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.962
with better tools for
walking alone at night.

00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:32.538
Open pathpro.tech in any phone browser.

00:00:32.578 --> 00:00:35.278
There's no app to install and no login.

00:00:35.318 --> 00:00:39.817
Two taps take you from opening it to a
route that starts at your GPS location.

00:00:39.857 --> 00:00:41.640
It works on desktop too,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.367
with keyboard and screen-reader
labels and large touch targets,

00:00:45.407 --> 00:00:48.264
and your walking patterns
stay on your phone.

00:00:48.425 --> 00:00:52.100
Here's Klaus to Midtown MARTA at
10:30 on a rainy Friday night.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.695
The teal PathPro route is about four
minutes longer than the fastest walk,

00:00:56.735 --> 00:00:59.831
with 54% less traffic risk.

00:01:00.073 --> 00:01:03.847
Tap Why, and it names the
high-risk stretches it avoids.

00:01:03.887 --> 00:01:07.434
Tap Listen, and ElevenLabs reads it aloud.

00:01:07.674 --> 00:01:13.855
<i>The PathPro route adds 4.2 minutes</i>
<i>and cuts traffic-risk exposure 54%…</i>

00:01:14.055 --> 00:01:17.208
Start navigation, and
PathPro walks with you,

00:01:17.248 --> 00:01:20.611
speaking up before each
high-traffic-risk crossing.

00:01:20.651 --> 00:01:24.767
<i>High traffic risk ahead. Fowler Street</i>
<i>Northwest and Ferst Drive Northwest,</i>

00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:26.860
<i>in 250 m.</i>

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.317
On a long walk, like Georgia Tech to Inman
Park, PathPro offers a faster option:

00:01:32.357 --> 00:01:36.113
walk 17 minutes to Midtown
station and take MARTA.

00:01:36.153 --> 00:01:39.167
Or switch to Bike, E-bike, or Scooter.

00:01:39.207 --> 00:01:45.419
This ride takes 27 minutes, with 72%
less traffic risk than the fastest ride.

00:01:45.577 --> 00:01:48.155
Walking at night is
about more than traffic.

00:01:48.195 --> 00:01:53.420
Personal-safety mode adds street
lighting, foot traffic, and help points,

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.323
including Georgia Tech's
blue-light phones.

00:01:56.363 --> 00:01:59.676
Reported crimes against
persons are informational only,

00:01:59.716 --> 00:02:03.468
shown with a fairness note, and
never used to choose routes.

00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:09.466
PathPro is for anyone walking or riding
alone at night: women and girls, students,

00:02:09.506 --> 00:02:13.053
people who rely on MARTA
instead of a car, older adults,

00:02:13.093 --> 00:02:15.364
and people on bikes and scooters.

00:02:15.404 --> 00:02:18.266
Choose well-lit and
busier streets after dark,

00:02:18.306 --> 00:02:22.097
with help points like Georgia Tech's
blue-light phones along the way.

00:02:22.137 --> 00:02:25.557
Share my walk lets a friend follow
along, and if you're running late,

00:02:25.597 --> 00:02:29.179
PathPro checks in, with 911 one tap away.

00:02:29.219 --> 00:02:32.758
And voice alerts keep your
eyes up, not on the screen.

00:02:32.798 --> 00:02:33.437
On desktop,

00:02:33.477 --> 00:02:38.932
Risk Tides re-scores about 50,000 Atlanta
streets for every hour and weather,

00:02:38.972 --> 00:02:42.720
on one citywide scale. Watch
corridors light up after dark,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.570
and again when the pavement turns wet.

00:02:45.964 --> 00:02:49.539
City Pulse scores all
3,537 areas of the city,

00:02:49.579 --> 00:02:52.570
so any address gets a score.

00:02:52.947 --> 00:02:56.370
Does it work? We trained on 2020 to 2023,

00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:01.537
and tested on 543 pedestrian crashes
from 2024 the model never saw.

00:03:01.577 --> 00:03:06.923
The 10% of streets PathPro
ranks highest held seventy-four

00:03:06.963 --> 00:03:08.368
percent of them.

00:03:08.408 --> 00:03:12.157
The City's High Injury Network: 54%.

00:03:12.197 --> 00:03:13.907
Random: 12%.

00:03:14.168 --> 00:03:16.206
What does better ranking buy?

00:03:16.246 --> 00:03:16.984
For a city,

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:22.162
the same budget spent on 10% of street
length reaches 38% more of next year's

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:25.169
pedestrian crashes than
the High Injury Network,

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:29.384
and, for rides, about
60% more bike crashes.

00:03:29.424 --> 00:03:34.596
For a person, four extra minutes cut
traffic-risk exposure by more than half.

00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:35.456
Nationally,

00:03:35.496 --> 00:03:40.831
NHTSA puts the economic cost
of crashes at $340 billion in

00:03:40.871 --> 00:03:42.201
2019.

00:03:42.241 --> 00:03:47.962
And a new city needs one coverage
polygon, plus its public crash data.

00:03:48.002 --> 00:03:51.921
Under the hood, we clean a quarter
million public crash records,

00:03:51.961 --> 00:03:57.250
snap them to 50,000 streets, and
score each one by hour and weather.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.500
One bundle feeds a FastAPI
service and a React map.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:06.516
Vultr runs all of it: the API and
the site, on one VM in Atlanta,

00:04:06.556 --> 00:04:11.577
close to our users. Caddy adds
automatic HTTPS, systemd keeps it up,

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.070
and one script deploys it.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.764
Our domain is pathpro.tech.

00:04:16.804 --> 00:04:19.051
Say it out loud: path protect.

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:21.573
The .tech completes the word.

00:04:21.613 --> 00:04:24.197
Tiger Data is our system of record:

00:04:24.237 --> 00:04:28.934
over 220,000 crash rows
in a Timescale hypertable,

00:04:28.974 --> 00:04:33.160
a continuous aggregate behind each
street's crashes-by-hour chart,

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:38.742
PostGIS geometry, and a risk
grid of 9.5 million rows.

00:04:38.782 --> 00:04:41.993
MongoDB Atlas holds what walkers tell us.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:47.078
Street reports use a geo index for
map queries, expire after 14 days,

00:04:47.118 --> 00:04:51.025
and repeats become confirmations
in one atomic upsert.

00:04:51.065 --> 00:04:53.556
Shared walks expire in 6 hours.

00:04:53.596 --> 00:04:58.444
Geo plus TTL fits short-lived,
user-generated data.

00:04:58.484 --> 00:05:00.743
ElevenLabs gives PathPro its voice,

00:05:00.783 --> 00:05:04.360
for explanations and for
walk alerts like this one.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.516
<i>High traffic risk ahead. Fowler Street</i>
<i>Northwest and Ferst Drive Northwest,</i>

00:05:08.556 --> 00:05:10.610
<i>in 250 m.</i>

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:15.567
Explanations come from
Groq's GPT-OSS 120B,

00:05:15.607 --> 00:05:19.550
for sub-second answers,
with Gemini as the fallback.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:23.834
A validator rejects any sentence with
a number that isn't in the evidence,

00:05:23.874 --> 00:05:27.621
so the LLM never produces a risk number.

00:05:27.661 --> 00:05:31.986
That's PathPro: traffic risk you can
see, for every street, every hour,

00:05:32.026 --> 00:05:34.169
and every way you get around Atlanta.

00:05:34.209 --> 00:05:36.526
Try it at pathpro.tech.

00:05:36.566 --> 00:05:39.399
See traffic risk before you walk into it.
